# Pi creates runtime files inside its config dir. We commit
# only `settings.json` (no secrets) and ignore everything
# else so a fresh clone doesn't accidentally check in a
# session log or auth file.
#
# - sessions/  : per-pi-process session files (turn history).
#                Useful for resuming a conversation, but
#                noisy and not something we want in git.
# - auth.json  : API keys. NEVER commit. Use the
#                OPENCODE_API_KEY env var instead.
# - models.json: custom model definitions. We don't ship
#                any; the built-in registry covers the
#                providers we use.
# - bin/, git/, npm/, prompts/ : pi's extension install
#                dirs. Mirror the global layout but stay
#                local. Not relevant for this project.
# - .cache/    : misc pi caches.
sessions/
auth.json
models.json
bin/
git/
npm/
prompts/
.cache/
